# The additive structure on the units colimit `H2Units V`

Umbrella development: `Submission/Work/HassePrinciple/` (README §8.4 item 1, §10.4).

`NK.HassePrinciple.H2Units V = colim_L H²(LevelGroup V L, Lˣ)` is the filtered colimit of the
level cohomologies `UnitsLevelH2 V L = H²(LevelGroup V L, Lˣ)` along the transition maps
`unitsLevelMap` (`UnitsColimit.lean`).  Every level is an abelian group (`ModuleCat CoeffInt`, via
`UnitsLevelH2`), and the transition maps are *additive* — they are morphisms in `ModuleCat CoeffInt`
— so the additive structure descends to the colimit: two classes represented at finite levels `L`
and `L'` are added by inflating both to the join `L ⊔ L'` (the compositum, again a finite Galois
level of `K'/K`) and adding the two inflated classes there.

This file provides that additive structure as an `AddCommGroup` instance on `H2Units V` such that
the structure maps `H2Units.ofLevel V L : UnitsLevelH2 V L → H2Units V` are additive
(`exists_addCommGroup_H2Units`).

## The construction, and why it is not done by hand

The colimit `NK.BrauerTwist.LevelSystem.Colim` is a quotient of the disjoint union of the levels
by the equivalence relation generated by the transition maps
(`NK.BrauerTwist.LevelSystem.eqvGen_gen_iff` shows that, the finite Galois levels being directed
by `⊔`, two elements are equivalent exactly when they agree after inflation to a common dominating
level).  Rather than prove the abelian group axioms for the "join" addition by hand on that
quotient, we use Mathlib's generic direct limit of a directed system of *additive monoids*
(`DirectLimit`, `Mathlib.Order.DirectedInverseSystem` + `Mathlib.Algebra.Colimit.DirectLimit`),
whose additive structure (`DirectLimit.add_def`) is provided by Mathlib:

* `unitsLevelMapHom V h : UnitsLevelH2 V L →+ UnitsLevelH2 V L'` is the transition map, bundled as
  an additive homomorphism (it is a `ModuleCat CoeffInt`-morphism, so its underlying linear map is
  additive);
* `unitsLevelDirectedSystem V` records the coherence laws (`map_refl`, `map_comp` of the level
  system) in the form required by Mathlib's `DirectedSystem`;
* `unitsDirectLimit V` is the resulting direct limit, an abelian group (and in fact a
  `CoeffInt`-module) for free;
* `h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V : H2Units V ≃ unitsDirectLimit V` compares the two presentations of the
  colimit — a `H2Units.ofLevel` is sent to the class of the level representative, and the two round
  trips are immediate from the respective universal properties;
* the additive structure of `H2Units V` is the transport of the direct limit structure along this
  equivalence (`h2UnitsAddCommGroup`), which is therefore automatically an `AddCommGroup`.

The additivity of `H2Units.ofLevel V L` is then exactly `DirectLimit.add_def` transported along
`h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V`, i.e. the computation rule "add at the join" at `L = L'`.

This development is the units counterpart, in the form of an actual group *instance*, of
`NK.BrauerHasse.exists_add` and `NK.HassePrinciple.exists_add_local`, which exhibit the join
addition as a bare function on the global and local colimits.  Nothing in the construction is
specific to the units coefficients: the same argument, verbatim, gives the additive structure of the
`mu_p` colimit `MuColim p V` (whose level system `muLevelSystem` has the same shape) and of
`H2Profinite p U`, the only input being the two coherence laws of the level system.
-/

import Mathlib
import Submission.NK.HassePrinciple.UnitsColimit

open CategoryTheory

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 1600000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option warn.classDefReducibility false

universe u

namespace NK.HassePrinciple

open NK.BrauerHasse

variable {K K' : Type u} [Field K] [Field K'] [Algebra K K'] [IsSepClosure K K']

/-! ## The transition maps as additive homomorphisms -/

/-- **The transition map of the units level system, as an additive homomorphism.**  The transition
map `unitsLevelMap V h : UnitsLevelH2 V L ⟶ UnitsLevelH2 V L'` is a morphism in `ModuleCat
CoeffInt`, so its underlying map is additive. -/
noncomputable def unitsLevelMapHom (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    (L L' : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K')
    (h : (L : IntermediateField K K') ≤ (L' : IntermediateField K K')) :
    UnitsLevelH2 V L →+ UnitsLevelH2 V L' :=
  (unitsLevelMap V h).hom.toAddMonoidHom

/-- The transition map of the level system `unitsLevelSystem` and the bundled homomorphism
`unitsLevelMapHom` have the same underlying function. -/
theorem unitsLevelMapHom_apply (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    {L L' : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K'}
    (h : L ≤ L') (a : ↑(UnitsLevelH2 V L)) :
    unitsLevelMapHom V L L' ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L L').mp h) a =
      (unitsLevelSystem V).map h a := rfl

/-- **The level system is a directed system of additive monoids.**  The coherence laws are those of
the level system (`LevelSystem.map_refl`, `LevelSystem.map_comp`), read through
`unitsLevelMapHom_apply`. -/
instance unitsLevelDirectedSystem (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) :
    DirectedSystem (fun L => (UnitsLevelH2 V L : Type u))
      (fun i j h => ⇑(unitsLevelMapHom V i j
        ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff i j).mp h))) where
  map_self := by
    intro i x
    rw [unitsLevelMapHom_apply]
    exact (unitsLevelSystem V).map_refl i x
  map_map := by
    intro k j i hij hjk x
    rw [unitsLevelMapHom_apply, unitsLevelMapHom_apply, unitsLevelMapHom_apply]
    exact (unitsLevelSystem V).map_comp hij hjk x

/-! ## The direct limit of the level cohomologies -/

/-- **The additive direct limit of the units level system**: `colim_L H²(LevelGroup V L, Lˣ)`,
presented as Mathlib's `DirectLimit` of the directed system of the level abelian groups along the
(fundamentally additive) transition maps `unitsLevelMapHom`.  It carries the direct limit additive
structure, and `DirectLimit.add_def` computes the sum of two classes of a common level. -/
noncomputable abbrev unitsDirectLimit (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) : Type u :=
  DirectLimit (fun L => (UnitsLevelH2 V L : Type u))
    (fun L L' h => unitsLevelMapHom V L L'
      ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L L').mp h))

/-! ## Comparison with the hand-made colimit `H2Units V` -/

/-- **The comparison between the two presentations of the colimit**: the hand-made colimit
`H2Units V = (unitsLevelSystem V).Colim` is equivalent to the additive direct limit
`unitsDirectLimit V`.  On level representatives the map is the identity. -/
noncomputable def h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) :
    H2Units V ≃ unitsDirectLimit V where
  toFun := (unitsLevelSystem V).lift (fun L a => (⟦⟨L, a⟩⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V)) (by
    intro L L' h a
    exact (DirectLimit.eq_of_le (F := fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))
      (f := fun M M' h => unitsLevelMapHom V M M'
        ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff M M').mp h))
      (⟨L, a⟩ : Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u)) L' h).symm)
  invFun := DirectLimit.lift
    (fun L L' h => unitsLevelMapHom V L L' ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L L').mp h))
    (fun L a => H2Units.ofLevel V L a) (by
      intro i j h x
      rw [unitsLevelMapHom_apply]
      exact ((unitsLevelSystem V).ofLevel_map h x).symm)
  left_inv := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨L, a, rfl⟩ := (unitsLevelSystem V).ofLevel_surjective x
    rfl
  right_inv := by
    intro y
    induction y using DirectLimit.induction with
    | _ i x => rfl

/-- The computation rule of the comparison on level representatives: the structure map
`H2Units.ofLevel` corresponds to the class of the level representative in the direct limit. -/
theorem h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K') (a : UnitsLevelH2 V L) :
    h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L a) = ⟦⟨L, a⟩⟧ := rfl

/-- The computation rule of the inverse comparison on level representatives. -/
theorem h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_symm_mk (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K') (a : UnitsLevelH2 V L) :
    (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (⟦⟨L, a⟩⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V) =
      H2Units.ofLevel V L a := rfl

/-! ## The additive structure on `H2Units V` -/

/-- **The additive structure on the units colimit `H2Units V`**, obtained by transporting the direct
limit additive structure along `h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit`.  The underlying operations are therefore
`x + y = e.symm (e x + e y)`, `0 = e.symm 0`, `-x = e.symm (-(e x))`, etc., where
`e = h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V`.

This is the canonical abelian group structure on `colim_L H²(LevelGroup V L, Lˣ)`: two classes are
added by inflating them to a common level (the join of their levels) and adding there, see
`h2UnitsAddCommGroup_add_ofLevel` (the join formula) and `exists_addCommGroup_H2Units`. -/
noncomputable def h2UnitsAddCommGroup (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) : AddCommGroup (H2Units V) := by
  let e := h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V
  letI : Add (H2Units V) := ⟨fun x y => e.symm (e x + e y)⟩
  letI : Zero (H2Units V) := ⟨e.symm 0⟩
  letI : Neg (H2Units V) := ⟨fun x => e.symm (-(e x))⟩
  letI : Sub (H2Units V) := ⟨fun x y => e.symm (e x - e y)⟩
  letI : SMul ℕ (H2Units V) := ⟨fun n x => e.symm (n • e x)⟩
  letI : SMul ℤ (H2Units V) := ⟨fun n x => e.symm (n • e x)⟩
  refine Function.Injective.addCommGroup e e.injective ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · show e (e.symm (0 : unitsDirectLimit V)) = 0
    simp
  · intro x y
    show e (e.symm (e x + e y)) = e x + e y
    simp
  · intro x
    show e (e.symm (-(e x))) = -(e x)
    simp
  · intro x y
    show e (e.symm (e x - e y)) = e x - e y
    simp
  · intro x n
    show e (e.symm (n • e x)) = n • e x
    simp
  · intro x n
    show e (e.symm (n • e x)) = n • e x
    simp

/-- The defining equation of the addition on `H2Units V`: it is the transport along
`h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V` of the direct limit addition. -/
theorem h2UnitsAddCommGroup_add_def (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) (x y : H2Units V) :
    (letI := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V; x + y = (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm
      ((h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V) x + (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V) y)) := rfl

/-- The defining equation of the zero of `H2Units V`. -/
theorem h2UnitsAddCommGroup_zero_def (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) :
    (letI := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V; (0 : H2Units V)) =
      (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm 0 := rfl

/-- The defining equation of the negation on `H2Units V`. -/
theorem h2UnitsAddCommGroup_neg_def (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K)) (x : H2Units V) :
    (letI := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V; -x) =
      (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (-(h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V x)) := rfl

/-! ## The addition on level representatives: the join formula -/

/-- **Addition in the direct limit at a common dominating level.**  Two classes of the direct limit
represented at levels `L` and `L'` may be added after moving both to any common upper bound `M` of
`L` and `L'`: the sum is the class at `M` of the sum of the two inflated classes. -/
private lemma directLimit_add_of_le (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    {L L' M : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K'} (h₁ : L ≤ M) (h₂ : L' ≤ M)
    (a : UnitsLevelH2 V L) (b : UnitsLevelH2 V L') :
    (⟦(⟨L, a⟩ : Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V) +
        (⟦(⟨L', b⟩ : Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V) =
      ⟦(⟨M, unitsLevelMapHom V L M ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L M).mp h₁) a +
          unitsLevelMapHom V L' M ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' M).mp h₂) b⟩ :
        Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ := by
  rw [show (⟦(⟨L, a⟩ : Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V) =
      ⟦(⟨M, unitsLevelMapHom V L M ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L M).mp h₁) a⟩ :
        Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ from
      DirectLimit.eq_of_le (F := fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))
        (f := fun M M' h => unitsLevelMapHom V M M'
          ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff M M').mp h)) ⟨L, a⟩ M h₁,
    show (⟦(⟨L', b⟩ : Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ : unitsDirectLimit V) =
      ⟦(⟨M, unitsLevelMapHom V L' M ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' M).mp h₂) b⟩ :
        Sigma fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))⟧ from
      DirectLimit.eq_of_le (F := fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u))
        (f := fun M M' h => unitsLevelMapHom V M M'
          ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff M M').mp h)) ⟨L', b⟩ M h₂]
  exact DirectLimit.add_def (G := fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u)) M _ _

/-- **The sum of two classes of `H2Units V` represented at the levels `L`, `L'` is computed at the
join `L ⊔ L'`**: both classes are inflated to the join — the compositum of the two levels, again a
finite Galois level of `K'/K`, which dominates both — and added there.  This shows that the additive
structure of `exists_addCommGroup_H2Units` is the canonical one on the filtered colimit.

The inflation `L → L ⊔ L'` is `unitsLevelMapHom V L (L ⊔ L')` (see `unitsLevelMapHom_apply`), i.e.
the transition map of the level system. -/
theorem h2UnitsAddCommGroup_add_ofLevel (V : Subgroup Gal(K'/K))
    (L L' : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K') (a : UnitsLevelH2 V L) (b : UnitsLevelH2 V L') :
    (letI := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V;
      H2Units.ofLevel V L a + H2Units.ofLevel V L' b) =
    H2Units.ofLevel V (L ⊔ L')
      (unitsLevelMapHom V L (L ⊔ L')
          ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_left) a +
        unitsLevelMapHom V L' (L ⊔ L')
          ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_right) b) := by
  let hAdd := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V
  have key : h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L a) +
        h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L' b) =
      h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V (L ⊔ L')
        (unitsLevelMapHom V L (L ⊔ L')
            ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_left) a +
          unitsLevelMapHom V L' (L ⊔ L')
            ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_right) b)) := by
    rw [h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel, h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel,
      h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel]
    exact directLimit_add_of_le V le_sup_left le_sup_right a b
  calc H2Units.ofLevel V L a + H2Units.ofLevel V L' b
      = (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L a) +
          h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L' b)) := rfl
    _ = (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V (L ⊔ L')
          (unitsLevelMapHom V L (L ⊔ L')
              ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_left) a +
            unitsLevelMapHom V L' (L ⊔ L')
              ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_right) b))) :=
        congrArg _ key
    _ = H2Units.ofLevel V (L ⊔ L')
          (unitsLevelMapHom V L (L ⊔ L')
              ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_left) a +
            unitsLevelMapHom V L' (L ⊔ L')
              ((FiniteGaloisIntermediateField.le_iff L' (L ⊔ L')).mp le_sup_right) b) :=
        Equiv.symm_apply_apply _ _

/-! ## The requested statement -/

/-- **`H2Units V` is an abelian group and the structure maps are additive.**

The units colimit `H2Units V = colim_L H²(LevelGroup V L, Lˣ)` of the level system
`unitsLevelSystem V` carries an `AddCommGroup` structure — the transport, along the comparison
`h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V : H2Units V ≃ unitsDirectLimit V`, of the additive structure of the
direct limit of the directed system `L ↦ UnitsLevelH2 V L` along the (additive) transition maps
`unitsLevelMapHom V` — for which the structure maps `H2Units.ofLevel V L` are additive:

`ofLevel (a + b) = ofLevel a + ofLevel b`  for `a b : UnitsLevelH2 V L`.

On the level `L` this is the computation rule `DirectLimit.add_def` of the direct limit: the sum of
two classes of a common level is the class of their sum.  Equivalently (by
`LevelSystem.ofLevel_eq_iff`) the sum of two classes represented at levels `L`, `L'` is computed at
the join `L ⊔ L'`, as in `NK.BrauerHasse.exists_add` and `NK.HassePrinciple.exists_add_local`. -/
theorem exists_addCommGroup_H2Units {K K' : Type u} [Field K] [Field K'] [Algebra K K'] [IsSepClosure K K']
    (V : Subgroup (K' ≃ₐ[K] K')) :
    ∃ (inst : AddCommGroup (NK.HassePrinciple.H2Units V)),
      letI := inst
      ∀ (L : FiniteGaloisIntermediateField K K') (a b : NK.HassePrinciple.UnitsLevelH2 V L),
        NK.HassePrinciple.H2Units.ofLevel V L (a + b) =
          NK.HassePrinciple.H2Units.ofLevel V L a + NK.HassePrinciple.H2Units.ofLevel V L b := by
  refine ⟨h2UnitsAddCommGroup V, ?_⟩
  intro L a b
  let hAdd := h2UnitsAddCommGroup V
  have key : h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L (a + b)) =
      h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L a) +
        h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L b) := by
    rw [h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel, h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel,
      h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit_ofLevel]
    exact (DirectLimit.add_def (G := fun M => (UnitsLevelH2 V M : Type u)) L a b).symm
  calc H2Units.ofLevel V L (a + b)
      = (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L (a + b))) :=
        (Equiv.symm_apply_apply _ _).symm
    _ = (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V).symm (h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L a) +
          h2UnitsEquivDirectLimit V (H2Units.ofLevel V L b)) := congrArg _ key
    _ = H2Units.ofLevel V L a + H2Units.ofLevel V L b := rfl

end NK.HassePrinciple

